"""Published callable profile used by code-producing operators."""

PROFILE_GUIDE = 'Use normal Python (python-v1), compiled and executed by Python itself. Write ordinary functions, classes, imports, loops, comprehensions, exceptions, closures and async functions as appropriate. No step signature, transition dictionary or hand-written state machine is required. Declare interface.entrypoint as the actual exported callable name; call_style is kwargs (a JSON object expanded as keywords), args (a JSON array expanded positionally), or value (one JSON value), default kwargs. args_schema describes that explicit invocation input. Helpers are ordinary Python imports and calls, e.g. from skills.helper_id import helper. Every current candidate module is available as skills.<component_id>, including existing source; inspect its actual callable interface. Declare any host function parameters explicitly in interface.host_bindings, mapping a parameter name to request or request_async. These capabilities accept a public request dictionary and return its original feedback; there are no implicit bot or task arguments. Return ordinary results. A fixture supplies args, expected return value or assertions, and requests=[{request,feedback},...] when external interactions are exercised. Preservation compares complete invocation results and observed requests, not internal execution steps. The host retains source versions, invocation arguments, function-boundary traces and request receipts. Process-loss recovery uses recorded facts and observations; ordinary Python stacks are not reconstructed and completed work must not be blindly replayed.'
